From: VIKINGYFY <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtdblock: silence NAND usage warning

OpenWrt supports devices which intentionally access small NAND partitions
through mtdblock. Avoid warning on every such access.

Signed-off-by: VIKINGYFY <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/mtdblock.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/mtdblock.c
@@ -261,10 +261,6 @@ static int mtdblock_open(struct mtd_blkt
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	if (mtd_type_is_nand(mbd->mtd))
-		pr_warn_ratelimited("%s: MTD device '%s' is NAND, please consider using UBI block devices instead.\n",
-			mbd->tr->name, mbd->mtd->name);
-
 	/* OK, it's not open. Create cache info for it */
 	mtdblk->count = 1;
 	mutex_init(&mtdblk->cache_mutex);
